# DevOven needs no configuration to run. Every tool computes in the browser,
# so `npm install && npm run dev` gives you the whole site with this file
# untouched. Copy it to .env.local only if you want one of the extras below.
#
# Required: nothing.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: feedback form delivery
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The "Feedback" link in the footer POSTs to /api/feedback, which forwards the
# message to a Telegram chat. Set both to enable it. Leave both unset and the
# form replies "Feedback is not configured on this instance" instead, which is
# the right state for a local checkout. Nothing else in the site depends on it.
#
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN: from @BotFather when you create a bot.
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID:   the chat the bot posts into. Server-side only; neither
#                     value is ever sent to the browser.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: analytics
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Your own Google Analytics 4 measurement ID (G-XXXXXXXXXX). Unset means the
# analytics script is never loaded and nothing is sent anywhere. If you fork
# this, use your own property, not someone else's.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: MCP server for AI agents (self-hosting only)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set DEVOVEN_MCP=on and /api/mcp serves every blocks operation as an MCP tool
# over Streamable HTTP, so an agent can encode, hash and convert through your
# instance instead of installing its own. /api/mcp/compact serves the same
# operations through two tools, for clients that cap tools per server. Unset,
# both routes answer 404, which
# is how the hosted site runs. If the instance is reachable by anyone but you,
# set a token too and the server requires "Authorization: Bearer <token>".
DEVOVEN_MCP=
DEVOVEN_MCP_TOKEN=
